<% title "Developer — #{@event.name}" %>

<%# FUIME: where an operator gets a key so their own software can sell for them.

    Written for a 16-year-old wiring an agent or a website into their business,
    which is why the page leads with a working example rather than a schema. The
    fastest possible path from this page to a paid link is the whole design
    brief.

    Nothing here suggests an amount, for the same reason the offers page does not
    (§8.3 D2). The examples use a price the operator has to replace. %>

<%= render "events/nav", selected: :api_keys %>

<h1>Developer</h1>

<p class="muted">
  A key lets your own software — a website, a Discord bot, an AI assistant —
  create payment links for your business. Give it a price, get a link you can
  send someone.
</p>

<%# ── The key it just made ─────────────────────────────────────────────────

    Shown once. Fuime stores only an encrypted copy and cannot show it again;
    see Fuime::ApiKey.mint!. Said plainly here rather than in help text, because
    a teenager who closes this tab without copying it has to make a new one.

    #create also paints this via turbo_stream so a Turbo form submit does not
    swallow the plaintext. The wrapper stays in the DOM even when empty so the
    stream has a target. %>
<div id="fuime-fresh-api-key">
  <%= render "fuime/api_keys/fresh_key", fresh_key: @fresh_key if @fresh_key.present? %>
</div>

<%# ── Keys ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── %>

<div class="card mb2">
  <h2 class="mt0 text-lg">Your keys</h2>

  <%= render "fuime/api_keys/keys_list", keys: @keys, can_manage: @can_manage, event: @event %>

  <% if @can_manage %>
    <%= render "fuime/api_keys/create_form", event: @event %>
  <% end %>
</div>

<%# ── How to use it ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    A copy-pasteable request, because that is what actually gets somebody from
    "I have a key" to "a customer paid me". `curl` first since it works from any
    machine with no setup, then the shape an agent needs. %>
<div class="card mb2">
  <h2 class="mt0 text-lg">Making a payment link</h2>

  <p class="muted text-sm">
    Send the amount and what it's for. You get back a link to send your customer.
  </p>

  <pre style="overflow-x: auto;"><code>curl -X POST <%= root_url.chomp("/") %>/api/fuime/v1/payment_links \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_KEY" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"amount": "35.00", "name": "Lawn mow"}'</code></pre>

  <p class="muted text-sm mt1">You get back:</p>

  <pre style="overflow-x: auto;"><code>{
  "id": "GKDm3dPQNHw2",
  "url": "<%= root_url.chomp("/") %>/pay/<%= @event.slug %>/lawn-mow",
  "amount_cents": 3500,
  "status": "published"
}</code></pre>

  <p class="muted text-sm mt1">
    Send that <code>url</code> to your customer. Other things you can do:
    <code>GET /api/fuime/v1/me</code> to check the key works, and
    <code>GET /api/fuime/v1/payment_links</code> to list what you've made.
  </p>

  <%# The one thing worth saying out loud to somebody about to paste this into a
      prompt. A key cannot move money — see CreateFuimeApiKeys — and knowing that
      is what makes it reasonable to hand one to a program at all. %>
  <p class="muted text-sm mt1">
    A key can only ask for money. It can't move your money out, see your
    ledger, or touch any other business. If one leaks, revoke it above.
  </p>
</div>

<%# ── What the software has been doing ──────────────────────────────────────

    The accountability half. An operator handing a key to an agent needs to see
    what it asked people for while they weren't watching, and this is the screen
    where a runaway key becomes visible. %>
<div class="card">
  <h2 class="mt0 text-lg">Links your software made</h2>

  <% if @links.any? %>
    <table class="w-full">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>What</th>
          <th>Amount</th>
          <th>Key</th>
          <th>When</th>
          <th>Status</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <% @links.each do |link| %>
          <tr>
            <td>
              <%= link_to link.name,
                          fuime_payment_page_path(event_slug: @event.slug, offer: link.to_param),
                          target: "_blank", rel: "noopener" %>
            </td>
            <td><%= render_money link.price_cents %></td>
            <td class="muted"><%= link.fuime_api_key&.name || "—" %></td>
            <td class="muted"><%= time_ago_in_words(link.created_at) %> ago</td>
            <td class="muted"><%= link.aasm_state %></td>
          </tr>
        <% end %>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  <% else %>
    <p class="muted">Nothing yet. Links your software creates will show up here.</p>
  <% end %>
</div>
